    ],
    "word_count": 51,
    "html": "<p>Berridge Spencer is a New Zealand investor and heir to the Caxton paper fortune built by his family. The son of John Spencer, he directs family investment interests through Clime and Windhaven. His businesses span private equity, property and wine, including Man O' War vineyards and a substantial Devonport commercial-property portfolio.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Berridge Spencer's Man O' War estate on Waiheke combines viticulture with a working farm. Its vineyard team mapped soils, slopes and weather patterns before selecting small planting sites. Red grapes went onto warmer, clay-rich ground; cooler volcanic sites suited white varieties. Steep terrain requires individual rows to be worked and grapes harvested by hand.\n\nThe family business has also developed ways for visitors to experience the land. A beachfront tasting venue serves its wines, while a forest route combines boardwalks and dual ziplines above the bay. Its Swiftsure range extends production to Marlborough and Bannockburn. The company also runs a bistro overlooking Buckingham Green in Arrowtown.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 93,
      "band": "high",
      "reason": "Owner identification is independently established; vineyard-manager interview and official current estate history support the operational details."
    },
    "source_ids": [
      "S2",
      "S6",
      "S7"
    ],
    "word_count": 106,
    "html": "<p>Berridge Spencer's Man O' War estate on Waiheke combines viticulture with a working farm. Its vineyard team mapped soils, slopes and weather patterns before selecting small planting sites. Red grapes went onto warmer, clay-rich ground; cooler volcanic sites suited white varieties. Steep terrain requires individual rows to be worked and grapes harvested by hand.</p>\r\n<p>The family business has also developed ways for visitors to experience the land. A beachfront tasting venue serves its wines, while a forest route combines boardwalks and dual ziplines above the bay. Its Swiftsure range extends production to Marlborough and Bannockburn. The company also runs a bistro overlooking Buckingham Green in Arrowtown.</p>\r\n"
  },
